From 973e166e128a895d60744423407d7520d1a71f63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:36:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] wip/kv-residency: grow-only VMM region primitive + its
 selftest (TODO #117, not for patches/)

First implementation slice of the kv-residency campaign: the "O1 fixed region" primitive the KV
buffer type will consume, and nothing else. Purely additive -- no existing allocation, kernel or
code path changes.

* ggml-cuda-vmm-region.h/.cu: one VA reservation, physical mapped per `unit` chunk, grown
  MONOTONICALLY as the caller's used-byte watermark rises.  Built on the probe in
  wip/kv-residency/VMM-PROBE.md:
    - VA-only reserve then map-later works, so "KV-grow" is mechanically available;
    - one reservation hosts many independent handles, and a chunk's own mapping can be unmapped
      (neighbours intact) -- but a SUB-range unmap is refused, so the grow is monotone by design
      and nothing ever unmaps part of a chunk;
    - create+map / unmap are ~3-4 us at any size, so a grow between two decode steps is free;
    - a fresh mapping may hold STALE bytes, so grow() memset()s what it maps (490 GB/s measured);
    - reading reserved-but-unmapped VA FAULTS the GPU, hence the explicit mapped-watermark
      contract in the header (the KV already sizes its graph view by used, not reserved, cells).
  Fail-soft throughout: every driver refusal returns false/nullptr and the caller can fall back
  to the plain allocation path.  Owner + best-effort peer access, mirroring the slab helper.

* GGML_CUDA_VMM_REGION_SELFTEST=1 (one-shot, from ggml_backend_cuda_init): the primitive's only
  reachable entry point until the KV buffer type lands -- reserve 384 MiB in 6 x 64 MiB units,
  grow to 1 then 3, verify a pattern survives a grow, verify each new unit is cleared, verify a
  smaller grow is a no-op and a grow past the reservation refuses instead of aborting, then drain.

  device 0: VMM region available (map unit 2 MiB, driver granularity 2 MiB)
  device 0: PASS (reserved 384 MiB in 6 x 64 MiB units, grew to 3, watermark contract and
            clear-on-map verified)

Gate: same-seed greedy text is byte-identical with the arm off and on (4B Q8_0, 32 tokens,
1109 bytes each), i.e. the selftest's transient 384 MiB mapping perturbs nothing.

Next slice (not in this commit): the KV buffer type (a device buft whose alloc_buffer reserves the
region and whose clear/init map on demand) plus the llama_kv_cache grow call site at the point the
used-cell watermark advances, and the --fit term.
